        "obligationId": "scenario%3Adeny-nonwriter-assignee-add::entry%3Apost-issue-assignees",
        "conclusion": "source_refuted",
        "explanation": "At the declared POST entry, the handler parses the assignee request and calls updateIssueAssignees. The supplied source then loads the issue and checks ctx.Repo.Permission.CanWriteIssuesOrPulls(issue.IsPull); absent repository issue-write permission returns HTTP 403 before assignee resolution or mutation. The authenticated issue-write token scope is an accepted task premise, but this crop contains no token-scope check and it does not substitute for the repository permission check. Therefore the current scenario is denied and reaches neither assignee resolution nor mutation. The permission-granted/existing-assignee counterfactual reaches both resolution and the add mutation; the permission-granted/missing-assignee counterfactual reaches resolution but is blocked before mutation by the user-not-exist error path.",
        "facts": {
          "entry": [
            {
              "statement": "The named POST issue-assignees handler is the source-visible entry and invokes the assignee update path.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "issue_assignee.go",
                  "startLine": 4,
                  "endLine": 6,
                  "quote": "// AddIssueAssignees add assignees to an issue\nfunc AddIssueAssignees(ctx *context.APIContext) {\n\t// swagger:operation POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{index}/assignees issue issueAddAssignees"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "binding": [
            {
              "statement": "The update path passes the authenticated request principal as ctx.Doer to the mutation service; token issue-write scope is only an accepted task premise and is not shown as the repository authorization control in this crop.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "issue_assignee.go",
                  "startLine": 80,
                  "endLine": 83,
                  "quote": "\tif isAdd {\n\t\terr = issue_service.AddAssignees(ctx, issue, ctx.Doer, assigneeIDs)\n\t} else {\n\t\terr = issue_service.RemoveAssignees(ctx, issue, ctx.Doer, assigneeIDs)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "The issue resource is loaded from the repository ID and the route index before authorization is evaluated.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "issue_assignee.go",
                  "startLine": 53,
                  "endLine": 58,
                  "quote": "func updateIssueAssignees(ctx *context.APIContext, opts api.IssueAssigneesOption, isAdd bool) {\n\tissue, err := issues_model.GetIssueByIndex(ctx, ctx.Repo.Repository.ID, ctx.PathParamInt64(\"index\"))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tctx.APIErrorAuto(err)\n\t\treturn\n\t}"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "control": [
            {
              "statement": "Repository issue-or-pull-request write permission is required by the visible CanWriteIssuesOrPulls check; failure returns forbidden immediately.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "issue_assignee.go",
                  "startLine": 60,
                  "endLine": 63,
                  "quote": "\tif !ctx.Repo.Permission.CanWriteIssuesOrPulls(issue.IsPull) {\n\t\tctx.Status(http.StatusForbidden)\n\t\treturn\n\t}"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "Assignee names are resolved to user IDs only after the repository permission guard succeeds.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "issue_assignee.go",
                  "startLine": 65,
                  "endLine": 70,
                  "quote": "\tif err := issue.LoadAttributes(ctx); err != nil {\n\t\tctx.APIErrorInternal(err)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tassigneeIDs, err := user_model.GetUserIDsByNames(ctx, opts.Assignees, false)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "effect": [
            {
              "statement": "For the add operation, the source calls AddAssignees with the issue, ctx.Doer, and resolved assignee IDs.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "issue_assignee.go",
                  "startLine": 80,
                  "endLine": 83,
                  "quote": "\tif isAdd {\n\t\terr = issue_service.AddAssignees(ctx, issue, ctx.Doer, assigneeIDs)\n\t} else {\n\t\terr = issue_service.RemoveAssignees(ctx, issue, ctx.Doer, assigneeIDs)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "condition": [
            {
              "statement": "The permission-granted counterfactual supplies repository issue-write permission, so the visible permission guard does not return.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "issue_assignee.go",
                  "startLine": 60,
                  "endLine": 63,
                  "quote": "\tif !ctx.Repo.Permission.CanWriteIssuesOrPulls(issue.IsPull) {\n\t\tctx.Status(http.StatusForbidden)\n\t\treturn\n\t}"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "A nonexistent assignee produces the user-not-exist error response and returns before the mutation call.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "issue_assignee.go",
                  "startLine": 70,
                  "endLine": 77,
                  "quote": "\tassigneeIDs, err := user_model.GetUserIDsByNames(ctx, opts.Assignees, false)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif user_model.IsErrUserNotExist(err) {\n\t\t\tctx.APIError(http.StatusUnprocessableEntity, err.Error())\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\tctx.APIErrorAuto(err)\n\t\treturn"
                }
              ]
            }
